  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Sun Pharma gets ratings boost from Moody's, S&P over $11.75-bn Organon bid",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/sun-pharma-gets-ratings-boost-from-moody-s-s-p-over-usd-11-75-bn-organon-co-acquisition-bid-126090800832_1.html",
      "description": "Rating agencies Moody's and S&amp;P assigned investment-grade ratings to Sun Pharmaceutical Industries -- India's largest pharmaceutical company -- over the proposed USD 11.75-billion acquisition of US-based Organon & Co.\nS&amp;P Global Ratings assigned a preliminary 'BBB+' long-term issuer credit rating, while Moody's Ratings assigned a 'Baa1' long-term issuer rating to the Indian pharmaceutical major. Both agencies have maintained a 'stable' outlook for the company.\nBaa1 and BBB+ are investment-grade credit ratings that indicate adequate payment capacity with moderate credit risk.\nThe rating actions follow Sun Pharma's binding bid in April 2026 to acquire a 100 per cent stake in Organon for an enterprise value of USD 11.75 billion. The transaction is expected to close by March 2027, subject to regulatory approvals.\nAccording to S&amp;P, the acquisition will bolster Sun Pharma's business position, almost doubling its revenue base to about Rs 1.3 trillion (around USD 14 billion) ..",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-08T13:36:16"
    },
    {
      "title": "S&P assigns 'BBB' rating to BoI on sufficient capitalisation, solid funding",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/banking/s-p-assigns-bbb-rating-to-boi-on-sufficient-capitalisation-solid-funding-126090800582_1.html",
      "description": "S&amp;P Global Ratings on Tuesday assigned 'BBB' long-term rating to Bank of India (BoI) on sufficient capitalisation, solid funding, and healthy liquidity.\nThe US-based agency said the ratings reflect the likelihood of extraordinary support for the state-run bank from the government, if needed.\nThe long-term rating on BoI is one notch above its assessment of the stand-alone credit profile (SACP) for the bank, S&amp;P said while assigning its 'BBB' long-term and 'A-2' short-term issuer credit ratings to the bank.\n'BBB' rating denotes adequate capacity of the institution to meet its financial commitments.\nThe stable outlook on long-term rating reflects our view that the bank will maintain its adequate capital position and solid funding and liquidity over the next two years.\n\"We base our view on BoI's very important role as a public sector bank in promoting financial inclusion through increased access to deposits and lending. The bank has very strong links with the government via the ...",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-08T08:06:29"
    }
